#X obj 513 11 noise.logistic;
#X obj 639 11 chaos.logistic;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 614 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 A non-interpolating generator based on the difference
equations:;
#X text 240 123 x[n+1] = λ * x[n] * (1 - x[n]);
#X obj 240 151 ui.link @background_color 0.90196 0.90196 0.90196
@title wiki: Logistic map @url
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Logistic_map;
#X text 240 172 By varying the parameter λ \, the following behavior
is observed:;
#X text 240 212 • With λ between 0 and 1 \, the population will eventually
die \, independent of the initial population;
#X text 240 252 • With λ between 1 and 2 \, the population will quickly
approach the value λ − 1/λ \, independent of the initial population;
#X text 240 307 • With λ between 2 and 3 \, the population will also
eventually approach the same value λ − 1/λ \, but first will fluctuate
around that value for some time.;
#X text 240 362 • With λ between 3 and 1 + √6 ≈ 3.44949 \, from almost
all initial conditions the population will approach permanent oscillations
between two values. These two values are dependent on λ.;
#X text 240 432 • With λ between 3.44949 and 3.54409 (approximately)
\, from almost all initial conditions the population will approach
permanent oscillations among four values.;
#X text 240 487 • With λ increasing beyond 3.54409 \, from almost all
initial conditions the population will approach oscillations among
8 values \, then 16 \, 32 \, etc.;
#X text 240 542 • At λ ≈ 3.56995 is the onset of chaos \, at the end
of the period-doubling cascade.;
#X text 240 582 • Most values of r beyond 3.56995 exhibit chaotic behavior
\, but there are still certain isolated ranges of r that show non-chaotic
behavior.;
#X text 240 637 Beyond λ = 4 \, almost all initial values eventually
leave the interval [0 \, 1] and diverge.;
